{{Documentation/Header}}
Renders a single birthday card: a 100&nbsp;px portrait, a linked page name, the birth date, and the utaite's age transition for the year.

It is normally called automatically by {{T|ProcessSingerPage/Birthday}}, which reads the values off a page's {{T|Utaite}} infobox — see {{T|ProcessBirthdayCategory}} for how the whole birthday system fits together. You can also call it directly with explicit values.

== Syntax ==
{{T|BirthdayEntry|block=1
|v1=name =
|v2=image =
|v3=birthyear =
|v4=birthmonth =
|v5=birthday =
}}

== Examples ==
=== With a known birth year ===
{{T|BirthdayEntry|_Y_=1|block=1
|p1=name = Example Singer
|p2=image = Template doc.png
|p3=birthyear = 2000
|p4=birthmonth = 10
|p5=birthday = 1
}}

=== With an unknown birth year ===
Passing <code>Unknown</code> suppresses both the year and the age line.
{{T|BirthdayEntry|_Y_=1|block=1
|p1=name = Example Singer
|p2=image = Template doc.png
|p3=birthyear = Unknown
|p4=birthmonth = 10
|p5=birthday = 1
}}

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>name</code> || – || Name || The utaite's page name. Used as the caption and the link target. || wiki-page-name || – || <span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">Required</span>
|-
| <code>image</code> || – || Image || Portrait filename, without the <code>File:</code> prefix. The literal value <code>Unknown</code> substitutes <code>Unknown.png</code>. || wiki-file-name || Template doc.png ||
|-
| <code>birthyear</code> || – || Birth year || Four-digit year. Set to <code>Unknown</code> to hide the year and the age line entirely. || number || – ||
|-
| <code>birthmonth</code> || – || Birth month || Numeric month <code>01</code>–<code>12</code>, converted to a month name. || number || – ||
|-
| <code>birthday</code> || – || Birth day || Numeric day of the month. || number || – ||
|}

== The age line ==
When a birth year is known, the card shows a transition rather than a single number:

: '''''(age last year)'' → ''(age this year)'''''

Both values come from {{T|Age}}. This makes the card read as a birthday greeting — "24 → 25" — rather than a static age.

